KG42.register("source_edge_archive-f24a790e70009e6013ebc0db",{"id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R009::E::v141-c-R009-E005","paper":"07-nash_bargaining","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","rule_ref":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R009","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R009-E005","source":"settlement.payment","target":"clearing.inter_area","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E18"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C003"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-6b28b8426784699b","target":"KG31-95bb253080ce87de","source_occurrence_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R009::V::settlement.payment","target_occurrence_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R009::V::clearing.inter_area","source_unit_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","target_unit_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-a-M01::clearing.inter_area","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Bilateral payment entries for every distinct pair of interconnected microgrids. | Determination of P2 payments for microgrids in M′ using the optimal P1 solution. | Eligibility of interconnected microgrids for P2 payment bargaining following P1 allocation. | Identification of the active trading group M′ and allocation of its members' benefits through P2. | Payments negotiated between interconnected microgrids. | The individual-rationality restriction on each microgrid's net trading payment. | The two-stage decomposition of NBP for interconnected microgrids; P1 covers all microgrids and P2 covers the trading set M′. | The virtual clearing house's payment-clearing service for participating interconnected microgrids.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"9926c91e7004ebdd678431460d50532beeda1a184ab4b1b34b59fd154c2fd9cc","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Following cost-minimizing P1, active microgrids in M-prime bargain over budget-balanced bilateral payments to maximize the product of gains relative to standalone costs, subject to individual rationality. Payments need not be linear in energy; this is not a per-kWh marginal or fixed midpoint price.","target_definition":"P1 jointly minimizes operating cost across microgrids with local balances, storage/demand constraints and bilateral antisymmetry of exchanged energy. ADMM implementation and virtual clearing house do not turn this into contract-network matching or an auction.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C003","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Participation in P2 payment bargaining is conditional on having a nonzero inter-microgrid trading allocation from P1. Scope: Eligibility of interconnected microgrids for P2 payment bargaining following P1 allocation. Condition: The microgrid has a nonzero energy trading vector e_i in the P1 solution, placing it in M′.","expression":"e_i ≠ 0 ⇒ i ∈ M′ (i participates in P2); M′ = { i ∈ M : i trades energy with other microgrids }, so i ∈ M′ ⇒ e_i ≠ 0; with e_i = { e_{i,j}^t, ∀t ∈ T, ∀j ∈ M\\i }; for j ∈ M\\M′, j does not participate in P2 and its operating cost equals its disagreement point C_j^{Non}.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment","clearing.inter_area"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R009-th-ei"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E17"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-7e85444402-p06-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"2652","section":"IV. PROBLEM ANALYSIS","anchor_text":"BP can be decomposed into two sequential subproblems on energy d- trading & scheduling and trading p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Theorem 1: The energy-trading bargaining problem NBP can be decomposed into two sequential subproblems on energy trading & scheduling and trading payment, denoted as P1 and P2, respectively. In the first step, we solve a social operating cost minimization problem P1 for the interconnected-microgrids system, which yields the optimal energy scheduling and energy trading for all microgrids. Those microgrids that trade energy with other microgrids form the set M′. In the second step, microgrids in set M′ bargain with each other to determine the energy-trading payments in P2."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-7e85444402-p06-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"2652","section":"IV. PROBLEM ANALYSIS","anchor_text":"BP can be decomposed into two sequential subproblems on energy d- trading & scheduling and trading p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"P1: Social operating cost minimization problem:\nmin ∑_{i∈M} CO_i(q_i, x_n, r_{c,i}, r_{d,i})\nsubject to (1)–(3), (5), (6), (8)–(11), (14), (15), and (17),\nvariables: { g_i, q_i, x_n, r_{c,i}, r_{d,i}, e_i, i ∈ M }.\nSolving P1 determines the optimal energy trading & scheduling {g_i^*, q_i^*, x_n^*, r_{c,i}^*, r_{d,i}^*, e_i^*} for each microgrid i ∈ M. If a microgrid i has a nonzero energy trading vector e_i, then it belongs to set M′, and will participate in the payment bargaining in Problem P2. For the non-trading microgrids j ∈ M\\M′, they do not participate in the payment bargaining and their operating costs are the same as the disagreement points C_j^{Non}."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Bilateral payment entries for every distinct pair of interconnected microgrids. | Determination of P2 payments for microgrids in M′ using the optimal P1 solution. | Eligibility of interconnected microgrids for P2 payment bargaining following P1 allocation. | Identification of the active trading group M′ and allocation of its members' benefits through P2. | Payments negotiated between interconnected microgrids. | The individual-rationality restriction on each microgrid's net trading payment. | The two-stage decomposition of NBP for interconnected microgrids; P1 covers all microgrids and P2 covers the trading set M′. | The virtual clearing house's payment-clearing service for participating interconnected microgrids.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R009-E005","source":"settlement.payment","target":"clearing.inter_area","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E18"]},"paper_scope_note":"Distinguish the interfaces of P1 dispatch, P2 payment, the actual transaction set, and the clearing institution; the same clearing institution does not mean that the variables of P1 and P2 can be merged."}});
